.TH MCGREGOR-WM 1 "November 2026" "mcgregor-wm 1.0"
.SH NAME
mcgregor-wm \- extremely minimal window manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcgregor-wm
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mcgregor-wm
puts a thin frame with a title bar around each window and provides
multiple desktops. It has no toolbar and no menus.
New windows never take the keyboard focus from the window you are
using: they appear with an orange title bar and are one Alt+Tab away.
Alt+Tab cycles windows on the current desktop in most-recently-used order.
This is the Slackware 3.6 (XFree86 3.3) build: titles use a Latin\-1
core font, and the X screen is treated as a single monitor.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Alt+Tab, Alt+Shift+Tab
Cycle windows, most recent first. Release Alt to choose; the mouse pointer
jumps to the centre of the chosen window (WARP_ON_ALTTAB). Escape cancels.
.TP
.B Alt+1..9
Go to desktop N (4 desktops by default).
.TP
.B Alt+Shift+1..9
Send the focused window to desktop N.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Alt+Left, Ctrl+Alt+Right
Previous or next desktop.
.TP
.B Alt+F4
Close the window.
.TP
.B Alt+F9
Iconify the window (Alt+Tab brings it back).
.TP
.B Alt+F10
Maximize or restore.
.TP
.B Alt+F11
Fullscreen or restore.
.TP
.B Alt+Return
Start xterm.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Alt+Shift+R
Restart in place, keeping X and all windows; also loads a newly installed
binary. Sending SIGHUP (killall \-HUP mcgregor\-wm) does the same.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Alt+Shift+Q
Quit.
.SH MOUSE
Click to focus and raise. Click the [X] on the title bar to close. Drag the title bar, or Alt+drag anywhere, to
move. Drag any edge or corner, or Alt+right\-drag near a corner, to resize. Double\-click the title bar to maximize;
middle\-click it to lower the window.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.mcgregor-wm/autostart
Run at startup if it exists and is executable.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Edit the settings at the top of mcgregor-wm.c and rebuild.
